  "nonogramTutorialSkip": "Skip",
  "nonogramTutorialWelcomeTitle": "Welcome to Pixel Nonogram!",
  "nonogramTutorialWelcome": "Let's learn the basic rules with a small 5×5 puzzle.",
  "nonogramTutorialInfoFree": "Free to play: every level is unlocked.",
  "nonogramTutorialInfoAds": "You can watch an ad (optional) for extra hints and magic wands. Sometimes an ad plays between levels.",
  "nonogramTutorialInfoPremium": "A one-time purchase turns off ads between levels and adds today-only hints and wands every time you check in.",
  "nonogramTutorialStart": "Start",
  "nonogramTutorialSwitchToFill": "Puzzles are solved by filling in squares. Tap the button below to switch to fill mode.",
  "nonogramTutorialClueIsCount": "The number tells you how many squares in the row are filled. This row has 5, so fill them all!",
  "nonogramTutorialDragNote": "Tip: you can drag your finger across the row to fill it in one go.",
  "nonogramTutorialEdgeCell": "The last square is already filled. The block of 4 must include it, so there is only one way to place it: fill the 3 squares to its left.",
  "nonogramTutorialMultipleClues": "More than one number means more than one block, with at least one empty square between them. 2 2 fits these 5 squares in only one way.",
  "nonogramTutorialClueOrder": "Order matters too: 3 1 means the block of 3 comes first, then the block of 1.",
  "nonogramTutorialColumns": "Columns have numbers too, read from top to bottom. Switch to X mode to mark squares that must stay empty.",
  "nonogramTutorialMarkEmpty": "Columns with a ✓ already have all their squares. Mark their remaining empty squares with an X.",
  "nonogramTutorialOneCellLeft": "The 1 in the last row now has only one place left. Switch back to fill mode.",
  "nonogramTutorialFinish": "Fill the last square to finish the puzzle!",
  "nonogramTutorialDoneTitle": "Well done!",
  "nonogramTutorialDone": "You're all set! On big puzzles, drag with two fingers (or from the empty space outside the grid) to move the board; the app will remind you on your first big puzzle.",
  "nonogramTutorialShowTechniques": "See solving techniques",
  "nonogramTutorialPlay": "Start playing",
  "nonogramGuideTutorialCardTitle": "Learn by playing",
  "nonogramGuideTutorialCardDesc": "Learn the rules, the controls and the main solving techniques step by step, by playing.",
  "nonogramGuideRoutineTitle": "Where to start",
  "nonogramGuideRoutineTip1": "Start with the big numbers. If a number is more than half its line, part of it is already certain (see technique 1 below).",
  "nonogramGuideRoutineTip2": "Solve the easy lines first: 0 means the whole line is empty, and if the numbers plus one gap between each add up to the line's length, it fits only one way.",
  "nonogramGuideRoutineTip3": "Mark squares you know are empty with X. An X is as useful as a filled square.",
  "nonogramGuideRoutineTip4": "Go back and forth between rows and columns. Every square you solve is a new clue for the line that crosses it.",
  "nonogramGuideRoutineTip5": "Never guess. When you're stuck, look for the line with the fewest unknown squares, or use a hint.",
