  "nonogramTutorialRulesDoneTitle": "You know the rules!",
  "nonogramTutorialRulesDone": "Next, let's practice the controls and helpers on another puzzle: drag to fill quickly, press and hold to mark, hints and the magic wand.",
  "nonogramTutorialContinue": "Continue",
  "nonogramTutorialLater": "Later, just play",
  "nonogramTutorialDragRow": "Tip: drag your finger across squares to fill them in one go. The top row has 5, so drag across the whole row!",
  "nonogramTutorialLongPressMark": "1 1 1 fits these 5 squares exactly, so the 2nd and 4th squares must be empty. No need to switch modes: press and hold each one to mark it with an X. A short vibration means it's done.",
  "nonogramTutorialUseHint": "Stuck? Tap the Hint button and the app fills 5 correct squares at random. You get 3 per puzzle.",
  "nonogramTutorialActivateWand": "The hint filled 5 squares marked with a star: they're locked and kept even if you restart. To reveal a whole row or column of your choice, use the magic wand: tap the wand button.",
  "nonogramTutorialPickWandLine": "Now tap the clues of the bottom row to reveal that row. You get 1 wand per puzzle.",
  "nonogramTutorialFinishTools": "Fill the remaining squares to finish. Drag down a column to fill faster.",
  "nonogramTutorialToolsDoneTitle": "Controls mastered!",
  "nonogramTutorialToolsDone": "Real puzzles are bigger, and most lines can't be solved at a glance. Next, learn the solving techniques on an 8×8 puzzle.",
  "nonogramTutorialOverlapSingle": "Look for big numbers first. The 6 fits these 8 squares in 3 ways, and each one blinks in turn. Squares lit in every way are filled for sure: fill the 4 in the yellow frame.",
  "nonogramTutorialOverlapMulti": "Same with several numbers: 3 3 needs at least 7 squares (3 + gap + 3), so it fits in only 3 ways. Fill the squares lit in all 3.",
  "nonogramTutorialFullRow": "8 in 8 squares: the whole row is filled. Drag across it.",
  "nonogramTutorialZeroRow": "0 means the row has no filled squares at all. Switch to X mode.",
  "nonogramTutorialMarkZeroRow": "Mark the whole bottom row with X. X's matter: they show the columns where blocks can't go.",
  "nonogramTutorialOutOfReach": "Now the columns. Column 2 is one block of 3 that must cover its 2 filled squares, so it fits in only 2 ways. Squares never lit can't be reached: mark them with X, and the same in column 7.",
  "nonogramTutorialBackToFill": "Look at column 3: it needs 7. Switch back to fill mode.",
  "nonogramTutorialExactSpace": "The X at the bottom leaves exactly 7 squares for the 7, so fill them all. Column 6 works the same way.",
  "nonogramTutorialFinishTechniques": "That's the routine: solve what you can in the rows, then in the columns, and repeat. Finish the mushroom on your own!",
  "nonogramPlayHintNothingToFill": "Every square that should be filled already is. Check for extra filled squares.",
